153	292,461,740,811	Fig. 153.	A Stonecrop flower, moderately enlarged: five narrow pointed sepals and five petals spreading from a short stalk, with slender stamens and the pistils standing in the centre.
154	147,953,867,1384	154. Petal. Stamen. Pistil. Pistil. Stamen. Petal. Sepal. Sepal.	Two parts of each sort, more magnified, set around the end of the flower-stalk in their natural order: a sepal lowest on each side, then a petal, a stamen, and a curved pistil innermost.
155	1556,1782,1741,1957	155. Pollen-grain.	A single round pollen grain of Mallow, highly magnified, its surface beset all over with bristly points.
